From: prplmesh OpenWrt package
Subject: [PATCH] controller: apply the steer list only to prplMesh agents

load_steer_on_vaps (hostap_iface_steer_vaps) names hostapd interfaces
of prplMesh agents. Other EasyMesh agents (e.g. a TP-Link RE500X) don't
report interface names, so is_vap_on_steer_list() rejected all their
BSSes and clients could never be steered to them. Always accept BSSes of
non-prplMesh agents.

--- a/controller/src/beerocks/master/db/db.cpp
+++ b/controller/src/beerocks/master/db/db.cpp
@@ -3150,6 +3150,14 @@
         return false;
     }
 
+    // The steer list names interfaces of prplMesh agents (hostapd ifnames).
+    // Other EasyMesh agents don't report interface names, so the list can't
+    // apply to them: their BSSes are always valid steering targets.
+    auto agent = get_agent_by_radio_uid(radio->radio_uid);
+    if (agent && !agent->is_prplmesh) {
+        return true;
+    }
+
     auto vap_name = get_radio_iface_name(radio->radio_uid);
     if (vap_name == "INVALID") {
         LOG(ERROR) << "vap name is invalid for bssid " << bssid;
